    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0592" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg492"/>

                <head>No. 357.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Reed.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 17,
                        1884</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 163.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 145 of the
                    21st ultimo, I inclose a a copy of a note<anchor n="*" xml:id="d357-f1"/> to the
                    Spanish minister here, touching the request of the consul of Spain at Baltimore
                    to be furnished with certificates of cargoes imported from Cuba, &amp;c., and of
                    the answer<anchor n="*" xml:id="d357-f2"/> thereto. * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
